<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ra</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Re</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ra, also called Re, was the ancient Egyptian god of the Sun, order, kings and the sky. By the Fifth Dynasty, in the 25th and 24th centuries BCE, he had become one of the most important gods of Egyptian religion, identified primarily with the noon-day Sun. According to Egyptian myth he carried the Sun across the sky in his solar barque by day and sailed through the Duat, the underworld, by night, defeating the serpent Apophis before returning at dawn. He was usually shown as a man with a falcon's head crowned by a solar disc, and he was merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horus">Horus</a> as Ra-Horakhty and, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> as Amun-Ra.</p></div>
